const char s422[] = "This is added to the target altitude in automatic flight. It can be used to add a global altitude offset to a mission";
const char s423[] = "ALT_SLOPE_MAXHGT";
const char s424[] = "Altitude slope maximum height";
const char s425[] = "This controls the height above the altitude slope the plane may be before rebuilding it. This is useful for smoothing out an auto-takeoff.";
const char s426[] = "ALT_SLOPE_MIN";
const char s427[] = "Altitude slope minimum";
const char s428[] = "This controls the minimum altitude change for a waypoint before an altitude slope will be used instead of an immediate altitude change. The default value is 15 meters, which helps to smooth out waypoint missions where small altitude changes happen near waypoints. If you don't want altitude slopes to be used in missions then you can set this to zero, which will disable altitude slope calculations. Otherwise you can set it to a minimum number of meters of altitude error to the destination waypoint before an altitude slope will be used to change altitude.";
