const char s10372[] = "Go directly to landing sequence via DO_LAND_START mission item";
const char s10373[] = "OnlyForGoAround";
const char s10374[] = "Go directly to landing sequence via DO_RETURN_PATH_START mission item";
const char s10375[] = "RTL_AUTOLAND";
const char s10376[] = "RTL auto land";
const char s10377[] = "Automatically begin landing sequence after arriving at RTL location. This requires the addition of a DO_LAND_START mission item, which acts as a marker for the start of a landing sequence. The closest landing sequence will be chosen to the current location For a value of 1 a rally point will be used instead of HOME if in range (see rally point documentation).If this is set to 0 and there is a DO_LAND_START or DO_RETURN_PATH_START mission item then you will get an arming check failure. You can set to a value of 3 to avoid the arming check failure and use the DO_LAND_START for go-around (see wiki for aborting autolandings) without it changing RTL behaviour.";
const char s10378[] = "Automatically begin landing sequence after arriving at RTL location. This requires the addition of a DO_LAND_START mission item, which acts as a marker for the start of a landing sequence. The closest landing sequence will be chosen to the current location. If this is set to 0 and there is a DO_LAND_START mission item then you will get an arming check failure. You can set to a value of 3 to avoid the arming check failure and use the DO_LAND_START for go-around without it changing RTL behaviour. For a value of 1 a rally point will be used instead of HOME if in range (see rally point documentation).";
const char s10379[] = "Fly HOME then land";
const char s10380[] = "Go directly to landing sequence";
const char s10381[] = "Enable - go HOME then land";
